      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "As a final example of likelihood-ratio tests, consider the general linear model (Chapters 8, 26, 27), $ \\mathbf{y} = \\mathbf{X}\\boldsymbol{\\beta} + \\mathbf{e} $, where we assume that the $ n \\times 1 $ vector of residual errors e is multivariate normal, with mean vector zero and covariance matrix $ \\mathbf{V} $, i.e., $ \\mathbf{e} \\sim \\text{MVN}(0, \\mathbf{V}) $. From Equation 8.24, the density function for e is",
